<title>GERMANY: East German May adjusted jobless rises 30,000.</title>
<headline>East German May adjusted jobless rises 30,000.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Labour Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> E.GERMAN UNEMPLOYMENT   May 97	 Apr 97	   May 96</p>
<p> Number (unadj)	    1.295 mln    1.315 mln	1.135 mln</p>
<p> Number (adj)		1.316 mln    1.286 mln	1.158 mln</p>
<p> Change (adj)		+30,000	+3,000	   n/a</p>
<p> Rate (unadj)		17.2 pct     17.5 pct	 15.2 pct</p>
<p> Short-time workers	53,997	 65,389	   79,842</p>
<p> Vacancies		   51,957	 48,473	   63,150</p>
<p> Change in number in work Mar 97	Feb 97</p>
<p>				 +17,000	-25,000</p>
<p>NOTE - Numbers in work data refer to change from previous month. Details on numbers in work to be released later today.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
